{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/792087-first-age-solar-s-hungry-ghost","id":792087,"title":"First age solar's hungry ghost","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-24T03:50:22-08:00","id":792087,"title":"First age solar's hungry ghost","content":"Has any book ever provided an example of the stats for the hungry ghost of a first age solar? Or has anyone ever found/created an example they're willing to share?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T13:05:53-08:00","id":792320,"title":"","content":"As you lose most of your cool stuff when you die, and as murder-hobo ghosts aren't renowned for their growth as a person, I'd just give them 5 in every attribute and ability with normal Hungry Ghost powers.<br /> <br /> But I generally see most Hungry Ghosts of great age and putrescence becoming Nephracks. So just use Neph stats? Or if you don't mind them being illiterate, use the Mask of Winter's stats from 2E Core (minus his Solar charms, because Hungry Ghosts don't get Solar charms). Maybe throw on an MA style or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T17:46:49-08:00","id":792448,"title":"","content":"In 1st edition, hungry ghosts of Exalts used the normal hungry ghost stats, but with fat bonuses to their soak, attack and damage based on their Essence. You could just use that. It's not particularly interesting though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T19:33:51-08:00","id":792493,"title":"","content":"I think they should be really hardcore. Tougher than the corebook Nephwrack.<br /> <br /> Burying Solars properly was supposed to be a big deal. The Sidereals and Dragonblooded didn't leave all that loot in the tombs out of generosity. They should have stats that make you think, &quot;it's worth leaving a dozen five-dot artifacts in a hole to avoid dealing with this thing&quot;.<br /> <br /> Each one should probably be unique. Most of their powers would be kill-rip-tear combat powers, but they'd have a few other tricks. Tracking down grave-robbers, blighting the land on which they walk, turning everyone within a hundred miles into an infertile insomniac, that kind of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T20:33:42-08:00","id":792517,"title":"","content":"Well. Solar Tombs are trying to prevent Ghost-ghosts. Deathlords, really. Hungry ghosts are just the feral, animalistic &quot;low&quot; nature - in theory, the same person could have both a Hungry Ghost and a regular one. For those of you more versed in Square RPGs than esoteric mysticism, think Heartless and Nobodies.<br /> <br /> But I still agree that a First Age Solar should precipitate a special case. Once, I ran a plotline involving a Lunar finding a Wyld Behemoth which magically preserved everything it swallowed, indefinitely. This included a Shogunate-era fortress (complete with guards, including several Dragon-Blooded), Aluveia of the Forge of Night, and Golden Tiger, the First Age Solar Mate to a PC Lunar. This last had died in the process of getting swallowed, but neither her soul nor her Exaltation had been able to leave the beast. In the intervening two thousand years, Golden Tiger's Hun and P'o souls had been able to keep deriving some power from the Exaltation, which remained partially tied to them in the absence of a new host.<br /> <br /> Stat-wise, this left the Hun Soul as a sort of mini-Deathlord - a mid-Essence Solar with Necromancy. Her enforcer was the P'o soul, which had crazy physical stats, but also had mastered Celestial Tiger and Solar Hero Styles (a sort of magical &quot;muscle memory&quot; from her life), and Hungry Ghost Style (because of course a Hungry Ghost Martial Artist gets that one).<br /> <br /> They proved a formidable tag team, right up until the Hun one cannibalized her &quot;other half&quot; to fuel her version of Birth of Sanity's Sorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T14:28:32-08:00","id":792833,"title":"","content":"Need a first age Solar hungry ghost? Try the Queen of Smiles, who is 12 feet tall, wearing dripping robes the colour of dried blood. Hands that are literally retractable blades. Darkly shining halo of blades that can fly about to rend soldiers by the army. A face not to be described in detail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1516-solarious","name":"Solarious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T17:11:05-08:00","id":792875,"title":"","content":"Assuming you're looking at 2E, I've got a pretty useful trick for it.<br /> <br /> The handful of times I've needed to make the Hungry Ghost of a first age Solar or something similar, I've found the method for generating your lower soul in the spell Links Born in Tumult (Black Treatise, Pg 42) to be really effective. It adds a hefty amount of punch to a Hungry Ghost, and then tweak and modify to your heart's content (Give it charms, arcanoi, etc, whatever you feel like throwing at your Circle.) The base stat-line alone means it'll hand anyone their own ass if they don't go in swinging hard with charms (nearly took out my players with one of these guys.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","user":"SamuraiMujuru","date":". 12-25-2015, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T17:50:24-08:00","id":792884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/792087-first-age-solar-s-hungry-ghost?p=792875#post792875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming you're looking at 2E, I've got a pretty useful trick for it.<br /> <br /> The handful of times I've needed to make the Hungry Ghost of a first age Solar or something similar, I've found the method for generating your lower soul in the spell Links Born in Tumult (Black Treatise, Pg 42) to be really effective. It adds a hefty amount of punch to a Hungry Ghost, and then tweak and modify to your heart's content (Give it charms, arcanoi, etc, whatever you feel like throwing at your Circle.) The base stat-line alone means it'll hand anyone their own ass if they don't go in swinging hard with charms (nearly took out my players with one of these guys.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome. Thanks! I probably won't add any extra charms as I'll be wrapping this thing in a Royal Warstrider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T18:45:12-08:00","id":792897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Burying Solars properly was supposed to be a big deal. The Sidereals and Dragonblooded didn't leave all that loot in the tombs out of generosity. They should have stats that make you think, &quot;it's worth leaving a dozen five-dot artifacts in a hole to avoid dealing with this thing&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm all for the idea that the tombs of First Age Solars were worth it to placate their mighty ghosts of whatever form, but I think some of the premises should be considered. For instance, is building a decent tomb worthwhile even if the hungry ghost is not a direct threat to some reasonably powerful Exalted, but rather to the surrounding locale and its inhabitants? Does it need to be difficult for a group of suitable Dragon Blooded to be capable of taking the thing down for that act, or the commensurate waiting, to represent a lower opportunity cost than making a good burial? Are they fast? Are they sneaky? For that matter, were the Artifacts you buried with them something that anybody else could use anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T22:22:45-08:00","id":792946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/792087-first-age-solar-s-hungry-ghost?p=792897#post792897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm all for the idea that the tombs of First Age Solars were worth it to placate their mighty ghosts of whatever form, but I think some of the premises should be considered. For instance, is building a decent tomb worthwhile even if the hungry ghost is not a direct threat to some reasonably powerful Exalted, but rather to the surrounding locale and its inhabitants? Does it need to be difficult for a group of suitable Dragon Blooded to be capable of taking the thing down for that act, or the commensurate waiting, to represent a lower opportunity cost than making a good burial? Are they fast? Are they sneaky? For that matter, were the Artifacts you buried with them something that anybody else could use anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, artifacts buried with a deceased solar are unlikely to be of use to any other Exalt without significant essence expenditure, plus, in the newly forming Immaculate Philosophy, the last thing you would want is for heroes of the new world to be wielding wonderous weapons attributed to the beings you're demonising (especially as many of them may be very hard to destroy, and locking them up inside ancient tombs might be a good way to go) - also, tombs don't NEED to be custom built. While grand mausoleum's may help to placate angry souls, they don't pass over to the other side, while aritifacts buried as grave goods can and do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T22:42:58-08:00","id":792951,"title":"","content":"Artifacts buried with a deceased Solar are extremely likely to be useful to another Exalt. Half the reason they're in the game is to serve as loot for PCs (who often have &quot;rights&quot; to the gear by virtue of being Solars/the reincarnation of the tomb's owner), so they've gotta be good loot.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm not inclined to give hungry ghosts subtle abilities. They're mostly murder-monsters, after all. But I do agree that they should have abilities that threaten the surrounding area. I gave the example of spreading infertility and insomnia, but really it could be anything. Maybe the ghost of a great Dawn general spawns an &quot;army&quot; of lesser hungry ghosts all over the surrounding country and has them &quot;declare war&quot; on the mortal population.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T23:31:50-08:00","id":792976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/792087-first-age-solar-s-hungry-ghost?p=792951#post792951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Artifacts buried with a deceased Solar are extremely likely to be useful to another Exalt. Half the reason they're in the game is to serve as loot for PCs (who often have &quot;rights&quot; to the gear by virtue of being Solars/the reincarnation of the tomb's owner), so they've gotta be good loot..</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I meant other Exalte TYPE - meaning of little use to the dragon bloods who sealed them in the tombs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T02:57:29-08:00","id":793036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I'm not inclined to give hungry ghosts subtle abilities. They're mostly murder-monsters, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div> I remember the way Gollum was discussed in The Fellowship of the Ring, in a way that made Gandalf and Aragorn very wary of the idea of him being unsupervised. All of that talk of a large region of Wilderland being on alert because of an invisible creeping terror that sneaks into nests and cots...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}